<%#
  Copy-to-clipboard button for any element rendered on the page.

  Wired by public/js/app.js: `data-copy="<selector>"` copies the target
  element's text (falling back to the button's own text). Used for attack
  payloads, request paths and hashes across the three labs and the forensic
  console, so every command shown in the UI can be taken to Burp without
  retyping it.

  Locals: target (required, an element id), label (what is being copied, for
  screen readers), text (button label, defaults to "Copy").

  No inline script: the Content-Security-Policy forbids it everywhere except
  the XSS lab's VULNERABLE mode, and this partial is not that.
%>
<button class="ws-copy" type="button" data-copy="#<%= locals.target %>"
        aria-label="Copy <%= locals.label || 'value' %>"><%= locals.text || 'Copy' %></button>
